{#
    One setting, anywhere in the application: an icon, what it is, what it currently says, and the
    buttons that change it.

        <twig:Ui:SettingRow
            icon="tabler:lock"
            title="{{ 'Password'|trans }}"
            description="{{ 'Change the password you sign in with'|trans }}"
        >
            <a href="{{ path('…') }}" class="btn">{{ 'Change'|trans }}</a>
        </twig:Ui:SettingRow>

    Add `status` to show a state badge under the description — a second factor that is on or off,
    a number of backup codes left, a device that is trusted:

        <twig:Ui:SettingRow
            icon="tabler:mail"
            title="{{ 'Email'|trans }}"
            description="{{ 'Receive codes by email when you sign in'|trans }}"
            status="{{ 'Enabled'|trans }}"
            statusColor="success"
            statusIcon="tabler:check"
            note="{{ 'Codes are sent to %email%'|trans({'%email%': user.email}) }}"
        >
            …
        </twig:Ui:SettingRow>

    It is deliberately the *only* way the platform renders a setting. A security row on the profile
    page and a second-factor row on the two-factor page are the same kind of information, so they
    are the same component — see the UI consistency rules in CLAUDE.md.

    Rows are `list-group-item`s, so they belong in a `list-group list-group-flush` inside a card:

        <twig:Ui:Card title="{{ 'Security'|trans }}" icon="tabler:shield">
            <twig:block name="body">
                <div class="list-group list-group-flush">
                    <twig:Ui:SettingRow … />
                </div>
            </twig:block>
        </twig:Ui:Card>
#}

{% props
    title = '',
    description = '',
    icon = '',
    iconColor = 'primary',
    status = '',
    statusColor = 'secondary',
    statusIcon = '',
    note = '',
    noteIcon = ''
%}

<div {{ attributes.without('class') }} class="{{ html_classes('list-group-item', attributes.render('class')|default('')) }}">
    <div class="row align-items-center g-3">
        {% if icon is not empty %}
            <div class="col-auto">
                <span class="avatar avatar-sm bg-{{ iconColor }}-lt">
                    {{ ux_icon(icon, {class: 'icon'}) }}
                </span>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="col">
            {% if title is not empty %}
                <div class="text-body">{{ title }}</div>
            {% endif %}

            {% if description is not empty %}
                <div class="text-secondary">{{ description }}</div>
            {% endif %}

            {% if status is not empty %}
                <div class="mt-2">
                    <span class="badge bg-{{ statusColor }}-lt">
                        {%- if statusIcon is not empty -%}
                            {{ ux_icon(statusIcon, {class: 'icon icon-sm me-1'}) }}
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {{ status }}
                    </span>
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            {% if note is not empty %}
                <div class="text-secondary small mt-2">
                    {%- if noteIcon is not empty -%}
                        {{ ux_icon(noteIcon, {class: 'icon icon-sm me-1'}) }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{ note }}
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# The actions. Wraps onto its own line below the description on narrow screens. #}
        {% set actions = block('content')|trim %}
        {% if actions is not empty %}
            <div class="col-12 col-sm-auto ms-sm-auto">
                <div class="btn-list justify-content-end">
                    {{ actions|raw }}
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
